course: dictionary
lesson: 8812
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job. Shed is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which job it is doing. «The bikes are kept in the garden shed.» Here a shed is a small building, often made of wood, where you keep tools or bikes.
explain: «Every spring, the takin sheds its thick coat.» Here shed is a verb, a doing word. To shed means to let something fall off. Trees shed leaves in autumn, and snakes shed their skin as they grow.
explain: Shed also has some special phrases. To shed tears means to cry. To shed light on something means to help explain it. Try swapping in your meaning: if «let fall off» or «cry» fits the sentence, you have found the right one.
fact: Shed can be a noun (a small building) or a verb (to let something fall off).
fact: As a noun, a shed is a small, simple building, often made of wood, in a garden or yard.
fact: As a verb, «shed» means to let something fall off, like a tree sheds leaves.
fact: «To shed tears» means to cry, and «to shed light on» something means to help explain it.
fact: Lizards shed their skin in pieces, snakes usually shed it in one long piece, and many geckos eat their old skin.
exercise: «The old bikes are kept in the garden shed.» In this sentence, what does shed mean? | To cry | To let something fall off | To help explain something | *A small building for tools or bikes
exercise: «Every spring, the takin sheds its thick coat.» What does sheds mean here? | *Lets its coat fall off | Shines a light on it | Builds a small wooden hut | Hides quietly from danger
exercise: «She could not stop herself from shedding tears when the kitten was lost.» What does shedding tears mean? | Looking for something under the cars | Hiding in the garden | *Crying | Building a shelter
test: «The lost cat was hiding quietly in a shed.» What is a shed in this sentence? | Something you drink from | *A small building in a garden | A kind of tree | A way of letting something fall off
test: «Lizards shed their skin in pieces.» Does shed mean keep safely, or let fall off? | *Let fall off | Sing loudly | Paint over | Keep safely
exam: «The new science book sheds light on how animals change their coats.» What does shed light on mean? | *To help explain | To give off shiny lamp light | To remove the light from | To make a loud noise
